repl[94] = ("Two boundaries limit what these",
"Two boundaries limit what these predictions can discriminate. First, the tests executed here separate the set-point architecture from site-specific, local-mechanical and joint-locus rivals, but not from a generic systemic rival in which any BMD-raising process also acts at the joint; that separation requires F2–F5 (volumetric decomposition, tissue enrichment, eQTL colocalisation, osteophyte-stratified outcome), unavailable with the present data. Second, P2's site-ordering clause is under-powered as a pairwise contrast (arms minus femoral neck +0.005, one-sided p=0.18), and P3 is not discriminating because a null colocalisation is predicted under any diffuse mechanism; one of ten pairwise contrasts (lumbar spine versus legs, p=0.022) reaches nominal significance — chance-compatible under Bonferroni but not excluded. Among the pre-registered predictions the genuinely discriminating one is P4, whose residual is resolved only by F2. The lowest-cost, highest-yield test is F5, pre-registered here: re-run with the OA outcome stratified into osteophyte-predominant versus joint-space-narrowing-predominant subtypes and test whether the BMD→OA estimate concentrates in the former; because osteophytes are the structural signature of the set-point, failure to concentrate would falsify the mechanism and concentration would confirm it against the same fracture positive control. F5 needs an OA GWAS with radiographic subtypes and is pre-registered rather than performed, so we claim no result from it.")

